     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><u><font size=\"2\">Providing a model using CDS:</font></u></div><div><u><font size=\"2\"><br></font></u></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\">ds(data, key=&quot;hr&quot;, adjustment=&quot;herm&quot;, truncation = 700,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\">             region.table = regions, sample.table = samples, obs.table = observations)</font></div></div><div><font size=\"2\">(</font><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px;white-space:pre-wrap\">AIC= 1911.957)</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></div><div><font size=\"2\">gives the following cluster size estimates:</font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\">Expected cluster size\r\n  Region Expected.S se.Expected.S cv.Expected.S\r\n  Total   6.613722     0.9939091     0.1502798</font></pre></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><u><font size=\"2\">Providing a model with the cluster size as a covariate:</font></u></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\">ds(data, key=&quot;hr&quot;, adjustment=&quot;herm&quot;, truncation = 700, formula = ~size,</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\">         region.table = regions, sample.table = samples, obs.table = observations)</font></div></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">(</font><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:Monaco;font-size:9pt;white-space:pre-wrap\">AIC= 1904.659)</span><br></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11);font-family:Monaco;font-size:9pt;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></div><div style=\"overflow:visible;min-height:0px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px\"><div><img title=\"Modify Chunk Options\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/5e455c374e0fd/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1&amp;view=1\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" style=\"margin-right:8px\"><img title=\"Run All Chunks Above\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/5e455c374e0fd/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%202?part=0.2&amp;view=1\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" style=\"margin-right:5px\"><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/distance-sampling/attach/5e455c374e0fd/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%203?part=0.3&amp;view=1\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" title=\"Run Current Chunk\" style=\"margin-right:8px\"></div></div><div style=\"padding-bottom:10px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px;min-height:1199px\"><br></div><div style=\"padding-bottom:10px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px;min-height:1199px\"><br></div><div style=\"padding-bottom:10px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:12px;min-height:1199px\"><br></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">gives the following cluster size estimates:</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\">Expected cluster size\r\n  Region Expected.S se.Expected.S cv.Expected.S</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" size=\"2\">  Total   4.693112     0.6531133     0.1391642</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><u>Questions/My Confusion:</u></font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">So, with MCDS is the estimated cluster size still worked out with regression?  Does this make sense when I&#39;ve used the cluster size as a covariate?  And if so, why are the cluster sizes predicted to be so much smaller when using cluster size as a covariate?</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\">Is there any good reading I can do around this subject?</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><br></font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Thank you</font></pre></pre></div></div>"
