   "subject": "[distance-sampling] Re: Cluster Size Estimate - MCDS vs CDS",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "\r\n\r\n  \r\n  <div><div>James</div><div><br></div><div>Good  question, particularly for those coming from the Distance for Windows software.  When using the R package Distance with clusters, the answer is that size-bias regression is not performed, regardless of whether there are covariates in the detection function.</div><div><br></div><div>Distance in R uses a Horwitz-Thompson-like estimator to estimate abundance.  The &quot;Expected cluster size&quot; reported by Distance in R is actually the ratio of the estimated individual abundance divided by the estimated abundance of groups.  You could have a look at the documentation for the function `dht` in the package `mrds` in R help for a bit more detail.</div><div><br></div><div>The estimates you provided give a good example of size bias.  The average size of groups detected in a survey is usually an over-estimate of the size of groups in the population.  This is because small groups at large distances are less likely to be detected and therefore appearing in your sample.</div><div><br></div><div>The computed expected group size in your model without size in the detection function is 6.6; however when group size is included in the detection function, there is acknowledgement of the influence of group size on detectability.  The computed expected group size is smaller in the model that includes size as a covariate; consequently removing (some/all) of the over-estimation of group size in the population that is present when the effect of group size on detectability is not considered.</div><div><br></div><div>Hope that helps you.<br><div><br></div><div><br></div><br><blockquote cite=\"http://d93...@st-andrews.ac.uk\" type=\"cite\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><div><br>\r\n      -------- Forwarded Message --------\r\n      <table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\">\r\n        <tbody>\r\n          <tr>\r\n            <th nowrap valign=\"BASELINE\" align=\"RIGHT\">Subject:\r\n            </th>\r\n            <td>[distance-sampling] Re: Cluster Size Estimate - MCDS vs\r\n              CDS</td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr>\r\n            <th nowrap valign=\"BASELINE\" align=\"RIGHT\">Date: </th>\r\n            <td>Fri, 12 Oct 2018 03:16:53 -0700 (PDT)</td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr>\r\n            <th nowrap valign=\"BASELINE\" align=\"RIGHT\">From: </th>\r\n            <td>James Richardson <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;james...@gmail.com&gt;</a></td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr>\r\n            <th nowrap valign=\"BASELINE\" align=\"RIGHT\">To: </th>\r\n            <td>distance-sampling\r\n              <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;distance...@googlegroups.com&gt;</a></td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n      </table>\r\n      <br>\r\n      <br>\r\n      \r\n      <div dir=\"ltr\">Sorry, message seemed to have been truncated:</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
