r\n              <pre style=\"line-height:1.45;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">Expected cluster size\r\n  Region Expected.S se.Expected.S cv.Expected.S</font></pre>\r\n              <pre style=\"line-height:1.45;color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\"><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"courier new, monospace\">  Total   4.693112     0.6531133     0.1391642</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\">\r\n</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><u>Questions/My Confusion:</u></font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">So, with MCDS is the estimated cluster size still worked out with regression?  Does this make sense when I&#39;ve used the cluster size as a covariate?  And if so, why are the cluster sizes predicted to be so much smaller when using cluster size as a covariate?</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">\r\n</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Is there any good reading I can do around this subject?</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">\r\n</font></pre><pre style=\"line-height:1.45;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Thank you</font></pre></pre>\r\n            </div>\r\n          </div>\r\n        </blockquote>\r\n      </div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
